{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your user reloads the page and the conversation is gone, because it only ever lived\nin memory. Or they open the app on their phone and none of it is there. Persistence\nfixes both, and it is two snippets: one middleware on the server, one option on the\nclient."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There is a second, separate problem: the socket drops while a reply is still\nstreaming. That is "},{"type":"link","href":"../resumable-streams/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resumable Streams"}]},{"type":"text","value":", a different\nlayer you can add on its own. Step 3 below combines them, which is what most apps\nend up wanting."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the provider sandbox is gone, the workspace files can also disappear. Use\nthe same persistence object with\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/portable-snapshots-configure","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep Files After Reload"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"install","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-persistence\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The client half needs no install. It ships in the framework package you already use\n("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-react"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-vue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-solid"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-svelte"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-angular"},{"type":"text","value":", or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-client"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wire this package's "},{"type":"link","href":"../getting-started/agent-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agent Skills"}]},{"type":"text","value":" into your coding\nassistant before you write any of it, then ask it for \"add chat persistence to this\napp\":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"npx @tanstack/intent@latest install","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run that after the package is installed. Intent scans "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node_modules"},{"type":"text","value":", so anything\nadded later needs another run."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-server-store-the-conversation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Server: store the conversation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withPersistence"},{"type":"text","value":" writes the transcript, run status and any pending approvals into\nyour own store. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence"},{"type":"text","value":" here is your adapter;\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./build-your-own-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"build one"}]},{"type":"text","value":" in about 40 lines, use a\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./build-your-own-adapter#third-party-adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"third-party adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":", or start with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"memoryPersistence()"},{"type":"text","value":" for local dev."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { persistence } from './persistence'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n    ...(params.resume ? { resume: params.resume } : {}),\n    middleware: [withPersistence(persistence)],\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-client-bring-it-back","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Client: bring it back"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two forms, and the choice is only about who owns the history:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence: true"}]},{"type":"text","value":" puts the server in charge. The browser caches nothing and\nasks the server for the thread on mount. Best for multi-user and multi-device apps."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence: <adapter>"}]},{"type":"text","value":" puts the browser in charge, with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"localStoragePersistence()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sessionStoragePersistence()"},{"type":"text","value":" or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"indexedDBPersistence()"},{"type":"text","value":". No server store needed."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Chat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    threadId: 'support-chat',\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    persistence: true,\n    // Or keep the transcript in the browser instead:\n    // persistence: localStoragePersistence(),\n  })\n  return <button onClick={() => sendMessage('hi')}>{messages.length}</button>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence: true"},{"type":"text","value":" the client needs one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GET"},{"type":"text","value":" to read from, which is step 3.\nWith a storage adapter you are done: reload and the conversation is there."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A long thread can page on hydrate. See "},{"type":"link","href":"./client-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client persistence"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nfor "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"history: { pageSize }"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-survive-a-reload-mid-answer","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Survive a reload mid-answer"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GET"},{"type":"text","value":" to the same route. It does two jobs, and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"if"},{"type":"text","value":" picks one per request:\nreplay a run that is still streaming, or hand back the stored transcript."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import {\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  memoryStream,\n  resumeServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reconstructChat } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { persistence } from './persistence'\n\nexport function GET(request: Request): Response | Promise<Response> {\n  const durability = memoryStream(request)\n  // A run still in flight: the client sent a resume offset, so replay its log.\n  if (durability.resumeFrom() !== null) {\n    return resumeServerSentEventsResponse({ adapter: durability })\n  }\n  // Otherwise return the stored thread, plus a cursor to any run still generating.\n  return reconstructChat(persistence, request, {\n    // WITHOUT this, anyone who guesses a thread id gets the whole transcript.\n    authorize: async (threadId, req) => ownsThread(req, threadId),\n  })\n}\n\nasync function ownsThread(request: Request, threadId: string): Promise<boolean> {\n  void request\n  void threadId\n  return true // replace with your session and ownership check\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" drives both halves for you. On mount it fetches the transcript, and if the\nserver reports a run still generating, it tails that run and the reply finishes in\nplace. Nothing else to wire, and a second device follows the identical path."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To make the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"POST"},{"type":"text","value":" resumable too, hand the same adapter to the response:\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toServerSentEventsResponse(stream, { durability: { adapter: memoryStream(request) } })"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"generation-and-sandboxes-use-the-same-idea","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation and sandboxes use the same idea"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (image, video, speech, transcription): the hooks take a\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence"},{"type":"text","value":" option too, boolean only, backed by a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generationRuns"},{"type":"text","value":" store. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./generation-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generation persistence"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./keep-generated-files","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep generated files"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to hold the bytes after the\nprovider's URLs expire."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sandboxed agents"}]},{"type":"text","value":": a run can outlive the tab and be adopted by another host.\nSee "},{"type":"link","href":"./build-a-sandbox-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build a Sandbox Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for what to\nstore, and "},{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/durable-runs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Durable Runs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for why."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"which-setup-do-i-want","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Which setup do I want?"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You want"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Turn on"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The conversation to survive a reload, nothing more"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step 2 with a storage adapter"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same conversation on another device, or after a server restart"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Steps 1 and 2 with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persistence: true"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A reload mid-answer to pick the answer back up"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Steps 1, 2 and 3"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A dropped socket to resume with the page still open"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../resumable-streams/overview","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resumable Streams"}]},{"type":"text","value":" alone"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To pause for a human approval and resume it days later"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Step 1 with an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"interrupts"},{"type":"text","value":" store"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sandbox files to come back after the provider sandbox is gone"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../sandbox/portable-snapshots-configure","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep Files After Reload"}]}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"where-to-go-next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Where to go next"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./chat-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat persistence"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the server middleware in full, including\ndurable interrupts."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./client-persistence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client persistence"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the modes, storage backends, and what a\nreload restores in each case."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./build-your-own-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build your own adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":": implement the stores against\nyour database and prove them with the conformance suite."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./controls","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Controls"}]},{"type":"text","value":": compose backends per store."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./internals","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How persistence works"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the two layers, thread and run identity, who\nowns history, and the middleware lifecycle. Read it when something surprises you."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"install","text":"Install","level":2},{"id":"1-server-store-the-conversation","text":"1. Server: store the conversation","level":2},{"id":"2-client-bring-it-back","text":"2. Client: bring it back","level":2},{"id":"3-survive-a-reload-mid-answer","text":"3. Survive a reload mid-answer","level":2},{"id":"generation-and-sandboxes-use-the-same-idea","text":"Generation and sandboxes use the same idea","level":2},{"id":"which-setup-do-i-want","text":"Which setup do I want?","level":2},{"id":"where-to-go-next","text":"Where to go next","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYour user reloads the page and the conversation is gone, because it only ever lived\nin memory. Or they open the app on their phone and none of it is there. Persistence\nfixes both, and it is two snippets: one middleware on the server, one option on the\nclient.\n\nThere is a second, separate problem: the socket drops while a reply is still\nstreaming. That is [Resumable Streams](../resumable-streams/overview), a different\nlayer you can add on its own. Step 3 below combines them, which is what most apps\nend up wanting.\n\nWhen the provider sandbox is gone, the workspace files can also disappear. Use\nthe same persistence object with\n[Keep Files After Reload](../sandbox/portable-snapshots-configure).\n\n## Install\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nvue: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-persistence\npreact: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nangular: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-persistence\noctane: @tanstack/ai-persistence\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThe client half needs no install. It ships in the framework package you already use\n(`@tanstack/ai-react`, `-vue`, `-solid`, `-svelte`, `-angular`, or\n`@tanstack/ai-client`).\n\nWire this package's [Agent Skills](../getting-started/agent-skills) into your coding\nassistant before you write any of it, then ask it for \"add chat persistence to this\napp\":\n\n```bash\nnpx @tanstack/intent@latest install\n```\n\nRun that after the package is installed. Intent scans `node_modules`, so anything\nadded later needs another run.\n\n## 1. Server: store the conversation\n\n`withPersistence` writes the transcript, run status and any pending approvals into\nyour own store. `persistence` here is your adapter;\n[build one](./build-your-own-adapter) in about 40 lines, use a\n[third-party adapter](./build-your-own-adapter#third-party-adapters), or start with\n`memoryPersistence()` for local dev.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { persistence } from './persistence'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n    ...(params.resume ? { resume: params.resume } : {}),\n    middleware: [withPersistence(persistence)],\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\n## 2. Client: bring it back\n\nTwo forms, and the choice is only about who owns the history:\n\n- **`persistence: true`** puts the server in charge. The browser caches nothing and\n  asks the server for the thread on mount. Best for multi-user and multi-device apps.\n- **`persistence: <adapter>`** puts the browser in charge, with\n  `localStoragePersistence()`, `sessionStoragePersistence()` or\n  `indexedDBPersistence()`. No server store needed.\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Chat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    threadId: 'support-chat',\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    persistence: true,\n    // Or keep the transcript in the browser instead:\n    // persistence: localStoragePersistence(),\n  })\n  return <button onClick={() => sendMessage('hi')}>{messages.length}</button>\n}\n```\n\nWith `persistence: true` the client needs one `GET` to read from, which is step 3.\nWith a storage adapter you are done: reload and the conversation is there.\n\nA long thread can page on hydrate. See [Client persistence](./client-persistence)\nfor `history: { pageSize }`.\n\n## 3. Survive a reload mid-answer\n\nAdd a `GET` to the same route. It does two jobs, and the `if` picks one per request:\nreplay a run that is still streaming, or hand back the stored transcript.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  memoryStream,\n  resumeServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reconstructChat } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { persistence } from './persistence'\n\nexport function GET(request: Request): Response | Promise<Response> {\n  const durability = memoryStream(request)\n  // A run still in flight: the client sent a resume offset, so replay its log.\n  if (durability.resumeFrom() !== null) {\n    return resumeServerSentEventsResponse({ adapter: durability })\n  }\n  // Otherwise return the stored thread, plus a cursor to any run still generating.\n  return reconstructChat(persistence, request, {\n    // WITHOUT this, anyone who guesses a thread id gets the whole transcript.\n    authorize: async (threadId, req) => ownsThread(req, threadId),\n  })\n}\n\nasync function ownsThread(request: Request, threadId: string): Promise<boolean> {\n  void request\n  void threadId\n  return true // replace with your session and ownership check\n}\n```\n\n`useChat` drives both halves for you. On mount it fetches the transcript, and if the\nserver reports a run still generating, it tails that run and the reply finishes in\nplace. Nothing else to wire, and a second device follows the identical path.\n\nTo make the `POST` resumable too, hand the same adapter to the response:\n`toServerSentEventsResponse(stream, { durability: { adapter: memoryStream(request) } })`.\n\n## Generation and sandboxes use the same idea\n\n- **Generation** (image, video, speech, transcription): the hooks take a\n  `persistence` option too, boolean only, backed by a `generationRuns` store. See\n  [Generation persistence](./generation-persistence), and\n  [Keep generated files](./keep-generated-files) to hold the bytes after the\n  provider's URLs expire.\n- **Sandboxed agents**: a run can outlive the tab and be adopted by another host.\n  See [Build a Sandbox Adapter](./build-a-sandbox-adapter) for what to\n  store, and [Durable Runs](../sandbox/durable-runs) for why.\n\n## Which setup do I want?\n\n| You want | Turn on |\n| --- | --- |\n| The conversation to survive a reload, nothing more | Step 2 with a storage adapter |\n| The same conversation on another device, or after a server restart | Steps 1 and 2 with `persistence: true` |\n| A reload mid-answer to pick the answer back up | Steps 1, 2 and 3 |\n| A dropped socket to resume with the page still open | [Resumable Streams](../resumable-streams/overview) alone |\n| To pause for a human approval and resume it days later | Step 1 with an `interrupts` store |\n| Sandbox files to come back after the provider sandbox is gone | [Keep Files After Reload](../sandbox/portable-snapshots-configure) |\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Chat persistence](./chat-persistence): the server middleware in full, including\n  durable interrupts.\n- [Client persistence](./client-persistence): the modes, storage backends, and what a\n  reload restores in each case.\n- [Build your own adapter](./build-your-own-adapter): implement the stores against\n  your database and prove them with the conformance suite.\n- [Controls](./controls): compose backends per store.\n- [How persistence works](./internals): the two layers, thread and run identity, who\n  owns history, and the middleware lifecycle. Read it when something surprises you.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Persistence Overview\nid: overview\ndescription: \"Set up persistence for chat, generation and sandboxes: one server route, one client option. Copy the snippets, then read the details only if you need them.\"\nkeywords:\n  - persistence\n  - durability\n  - rehydrate conversation\n  - page reload\n  - server authoritative\n  - client authoritative\n---\n\nYour user reloads the page and the conversation is gone, because it only ever lived\nin memory. Or they open the app on their phone and none of it is there. Persistence\nfixes both, and it is two snippets: one middleware on the server, one option on the\nclient.\n\nThere is a second, separate problem: the socket drops while a reply is still\nstreaming. That is [Resumable Streams](../resumable-streams/overview), a different\nlayer you can add on its own. Step 3 below combines them, which is what most apps\nend up wanting.\n\nWhen the provider sandbox is gone, the workspace files can also disappear. Use\nthe same persistence object with\n[Keep Files After Reload](../sandbox/portable-snapshots-configure).\n\n## Install\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nvue: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-persistence\npreact: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nangular: @tanstack/ai-persistence\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-persistence\noctane: @tanstack/ai-persistence\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nThe client half needs no install. It ships in the framework package you already use\n(`@tanstack/ai-react`, `-vue`, `-solid`, `-svelte`, `-angular`, or\n`@tanstack/ai-client`).\n\nWire this package's [Agent Skills](../getting-started/agent-skills) into your coding\nassistant before you write any of it, then ask it for \"add chat persistence to this\napp\":\n\n```bash\nnpx @tanstack/intent@latest install\n```\n\nRun that after the package is installed. Intent scans `node_modules`, so anything\nadded later needs another run.\n\n## 1. Server: store the conversation\n\n`withPersistence` writes the transcript, run status and any pending approvals into\nyour own store. `persistence` here is your adapter;\n[build one](./build-your-own-adapter) in about 40 lines, use a\n[third-party adapter](./build-your-own-adapter#third-party-adapters), or start with\n`memoryPersistence()` for local dev.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  chat,\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  toServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { withPersistence } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { persistence } from './persistence'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const params = await chatParamsFromRequest(request)\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n    messages: params.messages,\n    threadId: params.threadId,\n    runId: params.runId,\n    ...(params.resume ? { resume: params.resume } : {}),\n    middleware: [withPersistence(persistence)],\n  })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\n## 2. Client: bring it back\n\nTwo forms, and the choice is only about who owns the history:\n\n- **`persistence: true`** puts the server in charge. The browser caches nothing and\n  asks the server for the thread on mount. Best for multi-user and multi-device apps.\n- **`persistence: <adapter>`** puts the browser in charge, with\n  `localStoragePersistence()`, `sessionStoragePersistence()` or\n  `indexedDBPersistence()`. No server store needed.\n\n```tsx\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents, useChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nfunction Chat() {\n  const { messages, sendMessage } = useChat({\n    threadId: 'support-chat',\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n    persistence: true,\n    // Or keep the transcript in the browser instead:\n    // persistence: localStoragePersistence(),\n  })\n  return <button onClick={() => sendMessage('hi')}>{messages.length}</button>\n}\n```\n\nWith `persistence: true` the client needs one `GET` to read from, which is step 3.\nWith a storage adapter you are done: reload and the conversation is there.\n\nA long thread can page on hydrate. See [Client persistence](./client-persistence)\nfor `history: { pageSize }`.\n\n## 3. Survive a reload mid-answer\n\nAdd a `GET` to the same route. It does two jobs, and the `if` picks one per request:\nreplay a run that is still streaming, or hand back the stored transcript.\n\n```ts\nimport {\n  chatParamsFromRequest,\n  memoryStream,\n  resumeServerSentEventsResponse,\n} from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { reconstructChat } from '@tanstack/ai-persistence'\nimport { persistence } from './persistence'\n\nexport function GET(request: Request): Response | Promise<Response> {\n  const durability = memoryStream(request)\n  // A run still in flight: the client sent a resume offset, so replay its log.\n  if (durability.resumeFrom() !== null) {\n    return resumeServerSentEventsResponse({ adapter: durability })\n  }\n  // Otherwise return the stored thread, plus a cursor to any run still generating.\n  return reconstructChat(persistence, request, {\n    // WITHOUT this, anyone who guesses a thread id gets the whole transcript.\n    authorize: async (threadId, req) => ownsThread(req, threadId),\n  })\n}\n\nasync function ownsThread(request: Request, threadId: string): Promise<boolean> {\n  void request\n  void threadId\n  return true // replace with your session and ownership check\n}\n```\n\n`useChat` drives both halves for you. On mount it fetches the transcript, and if the\nserver reports a run still generating, it tails that run and the reply finishes in\nplace. Nothing else to wire, and a second device follows the identical path.\n\nTo make the `POST` resumable too, hand the same adapter to the response:\n`toServerSentEventsResponse(stream, { durability: { adapter: memoryStream(request) } })`.\n\n## Generation and sandboxes use the same idea\n\n- **Generation** (image, video, speech, transcription): the hooks take a\n  `persistence` option too, boolean only, backed by a `generationRuns` store. See\n  [Generation persistence](./generation-persistence), and\n  [Keep generated files](./keep-generated-files) to hold the bytes after the\n  provider's URLs expire.\n- **Sandboxed agents**: a run can outlive the tab and be adopted by another host.\n  See [Build a Sandbox Adapter](./build-a-sandbox-adapter) for what to\n  store, and [Durable Runs](../sandbox/durable-runs) for why.\n\n## Which setup do I want?\n\n| You want | Turn on |\n| --- | --- |\n| The conversation to survive a reload, nothing more | Step 2 with a storage adapter |\n| The same conversation on another device, or after a server restart | Steps 1 and 2 with `persistence: true` |\n| A reload mid-answer to pick the answer back up | Steps 1, 2 and 3 |\n| A dropped socket to resume with the page still open | [Resumable Streams](../resumable-streams/overview) alone |\n| To pause for a human approval and resume it days later | Step 1 with an `interrupts` store |\n| Sandbox files to come back after the provider sandbox is gone | [Keep Files After Reload](../sandbox/portable-snapshots-configure) |\n\n## Where to go next\n\n- [Chat persistence](./chat-persistence): the server middleware in full, including\n  durable interrupts.\n- [Client persistence](./client-persistence): the modes, storage backends, and what a\n  reload restores in each case.\n- [Build your own adapter](./build-your-own-adapter): implement the stores against\n  your database and prove them with the conformance suite.\n- [Controls](./controls): compose backends per store.\n- [How persistence works](./internals): the two layers, thread and run identity, who\n  owns history, and the middleware lifecycle. Read it when something surprises you.\n"}
